      },
      "text": "## Layer 1: The Triangle Mesh"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#007",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A mesh is vertices plus connectivity. The minimal modern form is an **indexed mesh**: a\nvertex array (positions + attributes) and an index array (triangles as vertex-index\ntriples)."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#008",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   VERTEX BUFFER                 INDEX BUFFER\n   pos        normal  uv         triangles (indices into vertex buffer)\n   v0 (...)   (...)   (...)      (0,1,2)\n   v1 (...)   (...)   (...)      (0,2,3)\n   v2 (...)   (...)   (...)      (2,4,3)\n   v3 (...)   (...)   (...)      ...\n   v4 (...)   (...)   (...)"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#009",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Why INDEXED: a shared vertex is stored ONCE, referenced many times.\n     non-indexed cube: 12 triangles x 3 = 36 vertices\n     indexed cube:     8 vertices + 36 indices -> far less data, vertex-cache reuse\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#010",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
