        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "### Vertex Attributes and the GPU's Vertex Cache"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#011",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A vertex is more than a position — it's a small struct of attributes, and the *index* buffer\nexists partly to exploit a hardware cache."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#012",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  A VERTEX carries (interleaved or in parallel streams):\n     position (xyz)   normal (xyz)   tangent (xyzw)   uv (uv)   color   bone weights..."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#013",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "POST-TRANSFORM VERTEX CACHE: the GPU caches recently transformed vertices by index.\n     a vertex shared by 6 triangles is transformed ONCE if its uses are close in the\n     index buffer. Reordering indices for cache locality (Forsyth / Tom Forsyth's\n     algorithm, or \"tipsify\") cuts vertex-shader work measurably."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#014",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "-> the index buffer isn't just dedup; its ORDER is a performance knob.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#015",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This is why mesh tools run an index-optimization pass: the same triangle list, reordered so\nshared vertices are referenced close together, hits the post-transform cache more often and\nruns the vertex shader fewer times. It's the geometry analogue of cache-friendly array\ntraversal — locality of *reference* into the vertex buffer."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#016",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "### Connectivity structures"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#017",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:computer-graphics:07-geometry, git-history:computer-graphics:07-geometry]",
        "canonical_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "concepts": "[triangle mesh, bezier curve, nurbs, subdivision surface, level of detail, mesh data structures]",
        "current_path": "computer-graphics/07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md",
        "id": "maxim:computer-graphics:geometry-and-meshes",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "computer-graphics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[geometry, meshes]",
        "section": "computer-graphics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Geometry and Meshes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Rendering only needs the indexed buffers, but *editing* (subdivision, simplification, normal\ncomputation) needs neighbor queries — \"which faces touch this edge?\" The **half-edge** (DCEL)\nstructure answers these in O(1)."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md#018",
      "path": [
        "07-GEOMETRY-AND-MESHES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
